WebZjs against the 2026-10 cohort: Ironwood (NU6.3) and NU7

Applies on top of 0003-librustzcash-2026-10.patch. Generated from the engine-port
working tree at a59b211 (make-celari-files.sh).

- webzjs-common: Pczt (de)serialisation returns errors instead of panicking; byte
  arrays deserialise from a Uint8Array too.
- webzjs-keys: pczt_sign signs Ironwood spends (Verifier::with_ironwood,
  Signer::sign_ironwood) with a CSPRNG seeded from the platform (SysRng); key types of
  zcash_keys 0.17.
- webzjs-requests: zip321 0.10 (Payment::new returns a Result).
- webzjs-wallet: zcash_client_backend 0.25 wallet API. propose_transfer spends from
  Sapling, Orchard and Ironwood (SpendPolicy::default()), the transaction version
  follows the target height (v6 once NU7 is active); propose_shielding; PCZT creation,
  proving (Ironwood proofs with the branch's Orchard circuit; the insecure pre-NU6.2
  circuit is refused) and extraction with per-bundle verifying keys; change and
  shielded transparent funds go to Ironwood from NU6.3. A browser clock (WebClock)
  and a CSPRNG (runtime.rs) for the backend's operations. Wallet summaries report
  ironwood_balance, locked and next_ironwood_subtree_index. Transaction history reads
  the new backend's tables. Keeps 0001's progress counters and 0002's memo;
  sync_progress() also reports the Sapling outputs, Orchard actions and Ironwood actions
  of the blocks the scanner trial-decrypted in the pass, and the Ironwood tree sizes
  before and after them.
- Review round 3 (PORT-NOTES Decisions 6-10): the history decides whether a send's outputs
  are known from the stored full transaction (a rescanned payment no longer reads as an
  internal transfer); NU7 boundary rules (sync before building across an epoch change or
  near an activation height, no build for the last 10 blocks of an epoch, pczt_send
  refuses a PCZT of the wrong branch or about to expire before storing anything); a sync
  pass frees each batch of compact blocks once scanned and ends at a batch boundary after
  its time budget (set_sync_pass_seconds, default 300 s; sync_progress().ended_early);
  after each pass the wallet's transaction data requests are served from lightwalletd
  (GetTransaction, GetTaddressTxids; pending_data_requests()); AccountBalance gains
  unshielded_pending; get_next_shielded_address returns a fresh Orchard+Sapling address
  without a transparent receiver, recorded in the wallet, while get_current_address keeps
  the full address. Native tests in webzjs-wallet/src/tests (mock lightwalletd, captured
  mainnet data from ../engine/zcash_client_memory/testdata).
- Review round 5 (PORT-NOTES Decisions 7 and 9 amended, 15, 17): a GetStatus answer counts only if it is the
  requested transaction; pczt_send reads the network tip again once it holds the
  database; nothing is built or sent for an upgrade's activation block itself; a sync
  batch is bounded by the bytes of its compact blocks (32 MiB, a download beyond 64 MiB is
  abandoned and continued in smaller batches; sync_progress() reports batch_blocks,
  batches_abandoned, largest_batch_bytes), so restores across the 2022-2023 spam era no
  longer exhaust wasm memory; db_to_bytes returns a buffer of exactly the wallet's size.

